      "generated_content": "THOUGHT: My fix is correctly implemented and addresses the exact issue described in the PR. The problem was that when using kmeans strategy, KMeans clustering doesn't guarantee that cluster centers will be in sorted order, which leads to unsorted bin_edges. Since `np.digitize` requires monotonically increasing or decreasing bins, this causes a ValueError.\n\nMy solution is to add `bin_edges[jj] = np.sort(bin_edges[jj])` right after computing the bin edges from the KMeans centers but before finalizing them with the min and max values. This ensures that regardless of the order of KMeans centers, the resulting bin_edges will always be properly sorted.\n\nThe fix is minimal, targeted, and maintains all existing functionality while resolving the specific issue described in the PR.\n</format_example>\n\n```mswea_bash_command\necho COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT && cat /testbed/sklearn/preprocessing/_discretization.py | grep -A 10 -B 5 \"np.sort(bin_edges\\[jj\\])\"\n```",
